Title: Shuffle
Credit: Written by
Author: Shahadat Hasan
Draft date: 22 July 2026
Contact:

FADE IN:

INT. HOUSE PARTY - NIGHT

SHAY (20s, neatly clothed)  squeezes past a crowded living room full of dancing students, lifting his flask overhead like it's a child in a flood. He reaches DEV (20s, tall, easy grin, slick hair) leaning into MAYA (20s, fashionable) who is laughing at something he said. KATE (20s, understated) looks on.

SHAY
Dev. It's midnight.

Dev's grin drops half an inch. 

MAYA
Midnight? What?

DEV
(groans)
It's a job we do for the science labs. We clean up after the experimental research group.

KATE
(to Shay, concerned)
They make you work in the middle of the night?

SHAY
Its the only time the labs are empty. No scientists, no experiments. But the hazard pay makes it twenty bucks an hour. 

MAYA
(scrunching face)
Only twenty dollars?

Shay lets that sit for a second, he turns back to Kate.

KATE
So are you going to leave now?

SHAY
(looking  to Dev)
Actually **WE** are going to leave.

DEV
It's the last night of semester. Everyone's taking off home tomorrow.

Dev puts his arm on Maya's shoulder and pulls her toward him.

DEV
Lets just enjoy it...

SHAY
Damn it, I would have just done the 8pm shift if I knew you weren't going to come.

DEV
So what, you're scared of working in the dark? Jesus if it's that bad I'll just come.

Shay looks embarrassed in front of the girls. Dev knows the silence is a standoff. Shay breaks first by exhaling. 

SHAY
Its fine, I'll do it myself. Probably get it done quicker without you anyway.

DEV
You're the best dude. I owe you one.

SHAY
You owe me like nine.

DEV
Ten after tonight. And I'm going to pay them all back. Trust me. 

He's already drifting away with Maya. He turns, walking backwards and motions a finger-heart with his hands. 

Shay exhales, looks at the party, then the door. He's halfway to it when Kate reaches for his shoulder from behind.

KATE
You're really not staying? 

Shay looks at her. A beat. It's a sliding doors moment.

SHAY
We told them we'd be there. Someone's got to do it. And its better than watching Dev try and flirt. 

KATE
That's a terrible reason

SHAY
(laughs)
Give me 30 minutes and I'll come up with a better one...

Kate smiles despite herself. Shay pumps one squirt of hand sanitiser onto his hands. Works it in. Opens the front door and walks out. The party ROARS behind him.

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. SCIENCE PLAZA - FREIGHT ELEVATOR - NIGHT

SILENCE.

WIDE SHOT. The entire scene plays in this frame.

A freestanding brick elevator stands alone in a concrete plaza between four dark buildings. Dimly lit by the full moon. Patterned red tiles with steel doors.

A RATTLE off screen. Shay enters, pushing a large grey rolling bin toward the elevator. Wheels CLATTER on brick.

The industrial lamp on top of the structure SLAMS on as he approaches. Old graffiti on the steel, two identical stick figures with smiles side by side. 

He pulls out a fist-sized key ring. Flips through the keys once. Twice. The JANGLE echoes. He finds the key and turns it in the wall panel.

A CLUNK inside the structure. A GRINDING WHIR below.

A line of yellow light from inside splits the doors. Top and bottom pull apart.

Shay wheels the bin in. Turns to face out. He looks tense.

The doors close, top and bottom. The light narrows to a line.

The plaza sits empty. The lamp HUMS. 

TITLE ON SCREEN: "SHUFFLE. Based on a true story."

The lamp CLICKS off, along with the ambient glow, casting the scene dark. Ominous tone plays.

INT. FREIGHT ELEVATOR - CONTINUOUS

Steel walls, scarred. One caged flickering bulb. 

Shay presses the button marked B2. The car LURCHES and descends. The motor WHIRS.

PING. Shay pulls out his phone. Text message.

KATE: "Come up with one yet?"

Shay grins. Types fast.

SHAY: "I'll have one in a few hours. Save me a drink and I'll trade you for it"

A small red heart emoji reacts on his message.

KATE IS TYPING... the dots pulse.  

PHONE SCREEN: signal bars drop. Three. Two. One. None

The dots freeze mid-pulse.

Shay watches the screen a moment. His smile fades a little. He puts in his earbuds and hits play. ROCK MUSIC.

The car SHUDDERS to a stop.

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

The doors grind open into BLACK.

The elevator's bulb throws a rectangle of light a few feet into a concrete corridor. Beyond it, nothing.

Shay backs out, pulling the bin, his music still playing. He stands at the edge of the elevator's light, half his face lit, half in dark.

He looks left down the corridor. Dark.

He looks right. Dark.

He pulls his earbuds out. And tilts his head to listen. SILENCE.

Above him, the ceiling fixture stays dark. He waves an arm. Nothing. He steps sideways, one big deliberate step.

A motion sensor CLICKS. The tube overhead stutters on. Then the next one down in both directions. 

Shay exhales and pushes the bin down the corridor. The next sensor CLICKS on ahead of him as he walks.

INT. B2 LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

A cramped room. One wall of dented steel lockers and a metal bench. A mirror, spotted with age, is bolted to the wall.

Shay yanks the pull-cord bulb. It swings slightly, shadows tilting with it.

One locker at the near side hangs open. Inside a wire hanger with a lab coat. Shay pushes it shut. The CLANG echoes.

Taped to the front of his locker door, a yellow post-it:

"SHAY. LAST ONE. PIKE EXPERIMENT WASTE FULL. LOCK UP AFTER. HAPPY HOLIDAYS. RAY"

Shay spins the lock combination without looking. It opens.

He replaces the lab coat with his own on the hanger.

On the wall above the bench, two laminated safety posters, sun-faded: "SHARPS BITE. CHECK EVERY BAG." Beside it: "GOGGLES ON AT ALL TIMES. NO EXCEPTIONS."

He puts on a pair of blue gloves, then a second pair over them. He hangs the safety goggles around his neck and sits on the bench.

AT FLOOR LEVEL: his shoe pushes into a blue paper bootie. The paper RASPS over the toe. He plants the one foot then the other. SHF. SHF.

He stands and takes two steps to the mirror. SHF. SHF.

In the smudged spotted glass, he takes his hand and wipes the mirror to see his face more clearly. He pauses for a moment.

He turns to a shelf by the door. A cardboard box marked "BAGS" in marker. He tips it toward him. Empty. He checks under the bench. Nothing.

SHAY
(under his breath)
Fucking hell, Dev.

At the end of the room, a heavy steel sliding door, streaked with rust and sealed with a padlock. Above it a decaying sign reads "SUPPLIES".

Shay flips through the key ring and unlocks it.

He grips the handle and hauls sideways. The door GRINDS along its track, a long metal SCRAPE that fills the corridor.

Beyond it: BLACK. The corridor light reaches a few feet in. 

INT. B2 SUPPLY ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Shay steps in. The darkness surrounds him. 

He walks a narrow aisle between shelf stacks, one hand trailing a shelf edge. His SHF. SHF. the only sound.

THUMP. Deep in the room. Ahead of him.

He stops. Silence. He holds his breath.

Then scampers toward the light. SHF. SHF. SHF. Faster.

His hand finds the wall. Slaps along it. Finds the SWITCH.

A single bulb stutters on, dim, halfway down the room.

At the far end: a cardboard BOX on its side on the floor, fallen from the top of a stack. Clear plastic DISPOSAL BAGS fanned out of it across the concrete.

Shay stares at it. Exhales.

He rights the box, and wedges it onto a lower shelf, pulling out two rolls of bags and tucking them under his arm. He switches off the light.

We look out from inside the room. Shay walks out and hauls the door shut. SCRAPE. 

CUT TO:

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - PIKE LAB DOOR - NIGHT

A grey steel door. A small sign box: "LAB IN USE." Unlit. Shay pulls out his keys, unlocks it and walks in.

INT. PIKE LAB - CONTINUOUS

Darkness. At the far end of the room, a fume hood HUMS and glows soft yellow light, a pipette rig inside it DRIPPING yellow liquid into a flask. 

No sensor click. Shay scans the room defensively. 

Without looking, he flicks the wall switch. Nothing. Down, up, down, up. The tubes STUTTER awake, half of them. The far end stays in the hood's yellow half-light.

Shay starts on the near side, lifting the full bags, zipties them carefully and places them into the bin.

The lights CLICK off, leaving just the hood's yellow glow.

SHAY
Oh, come on.

He waves an arm. Nothing. Steps left, steps right. SHF. SHF. Nothing. He uses his annoyance to mask his fear.

The HUMMING seems to intensify, drawing him closer and closer to the hood, until he is right next to it. As he peers intensely, the drips quicken, the yellow hue on his face. 

PIKE (O.S.)
What are you doing in here? Don't touch that.

The overhead lights SLAM ON. Shay spins. A man stands at the far end. PIKE (40s, unshaven, annoyed), a rack of tubes in one hand. 

SHAY
Jesus. I'm... emptying the waste.

PIKE
(curtly)
Then be near the waste.

Shay holds his look for a second. Then walks to the waste corner and starts working. Pike crosses to a coffee pot on the side counter. Picks it up. Shakes it. Empty.

PIKE (CONT'D)
Don't touch anything in here, **understand?**

He leaves without waiting for a response. 

SHAY
(under his breath)
Asshole.

Shay works the messy side. A bin labeled POWDERS emits a small puff of smoke as he carefully lifts it out. Then he repeats for a bin labeled: GENERAL. NO SHARPS.

He hauls the bag out one-handed, swings it up.

SHAY (CONT'D)
AGHH!

The bag drops as something stabs his hand. A glassy CLINK.

The lights CLICK OFF.

SHAY  
Oh, you've got to be fucking kidding-

He slaps the key ring down on the bench and frantically strips the outer glove. Then the inner. He holds his palm up to the fume hood's glow. A bead of blood, black in the yellow light. Panic sets in. He tries to squeeze out the liquid. Yellow and red gunk oozes out.

He rummages through the bin bag, finding a loose SYRINGE.

Shay slams the syringe into the red sharps container and snaps the lid shut, storming toward the door.

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

The door CRACKS off the wall as he shoulders it hard. 

He looks right. Dark. To the left, a far section is lit. A SHADOW slides around the corner. The section CLICKS off.

He looks at his WATCH: 2:00AM. He grimaces in frustration and reluctantly goes back in. 

INT. PIKE LAB - CONTINUOUS

WIDE, STATIC. MIRRORING THE OPENING PLAZA SHOT: the whole room in one held frame. The FUME HOOD is dead centre like how the elevator entrance stood. The soft yellow illumination coming from the bulb above, mimicking the light above the elevator housing. The rig inside it continues to DRIP.

Shay, small in the wide shot, works the room. He puts on fresh gloves from his coat pocket. He wheels the bin out the door, out of frame.

The door clicks shut and the room sits empty. The hood glows. The rig continues to DRIP.

The hood light CLICKS off. The DRIP stops. Silence.

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Shay walks back toward the locker room, pushing the bin.

AT FLOOR LEVEL: his feet, each step of his blue booties, trigger the sensor light above and make a shuffling noise.

SHF. SHF. 

Shay feels he is being followed. He stops. He tilts his head to hear. Silence. He is sweating more than before.

He walks again. Slow now. Deliberate. One step. SHF.

Another. SHF.

He lifts his foot. Holds it mid-air.

SHF. A noise is made while his foot is raised.

He slowly sets it down and turns around.

POV THROUGH GOGGLES: fog creeps in from the rims of the lenses, hazing the image. The far corridor sections go dark.

Shay rips the goggles down to his throat. Wipes his brow.

He looks down, a trail of blood drips extends down the corridor from his hand. 

He looks at his hand, the wound has bled through. The stain is dark. Almost black.

The lights pause at the blood and then start to click off quicker towards him.

He grabs the bin and RUNS.

INT. B2 LOCKER ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Shay slams through the door and pushes it shut. 

He rolls the bin onto the steel floor scale in the corner and leaves it there. 

Behind him unnoticed the readout climbs, settling on 11.8 lbs.

He turns for his locker and stops.

The near locker hangs open again. No lab coat inside anymore.

He SLAMS the locker shut. The CLANG rings. He turns to his own locker and spins the combination. Wrong. Again. Wrong. Finally he gets it.

He digs into his backpack. Pulls out a small antiseptic bottle, half-used, a packet of wipes and plasters. 

He strips both gloves off the wounded hand. The skin around the puncture is flushed, the puncture itself dark.

His panic rises, and he tips the antiseptic straight onto the palm, scrubs it in with a wipe with a plaster on top.

He breathes deeply. Tries to relax. He flexes his hand. And looks back at it. 

Thin dark lines are creeping out from under the plaster's edge, spreading across his palm. Shay panics, claws the plaster off, runs over to the utility sink in the corner and cranks the cold tap, plunging his hand under the running water. 


The water hits the drain clear. Then grey. Then BLACK. Thick black liquid running off his palm onto the white porcelain.


SHAY
(breathing fast)
What the fuck?! What the fuck?!

He rips his hand out. Stares at it. The water runs black and then stops. He backs off the sink and fumbles his phone out with his left hand. Shaking, he dials 911. 

NO SIGNAL. 

He hurriedly grabs his backpack from his locker, and shoves out the door half tangled in his lab coat.

INT. B2 Corridor - night

Shay breathes heavy as he runs around the corner down the corridor, the light outside the elevator dimly lit. He looks behind him as he reaches the elevator.

The wall panel key-hole fills our view. Shay searches inside his lab pocket. Nothing. He checks his jeans. Nothing. 

SHAY
Shit...

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - PIKE LAB DOOR - NIGHT

Above the door, the sign box: "LAB IN USE." LIT.

Shay stops. Stares at it.

He exhales through his nose, pulls back his shoulders and pushes the door open.

INT. PIKE LAB - CONTINUOUS

Dark. No one at the bench. No one in the yellow glow of the fume hood.

On the side counter, the coffee pot is full. Steam rises. He sees his keys on the other side of the room and inches towards them.

Past the fume hood, the far corner. The dark there is thicker. A shape. A coat rack. Maybe nothing.

He stares into the corner. It doesn't resolve. The different hues of darkness blend. An outline of a figure. He leans forward.

DRIP. His eyes flick to the rig. 

Suddenly a noise from the corner: SHF.

His eyes snap back. The corner. The dark. Something is there.

SHF. SHF. SHF! SHF!

Shay screams, grabs the keys from the bench and scrambles out the door.

INT. B2 CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

He runs to the end of the hallway where the elevator entrance is. He looks back as the lights start to switch off. 

He fumbles with his keychain at the panel, stabs the key at the slot, misses, scrapes, gets it in. Turns it.

Above the doors, the floor indicator glows: **1.**

A CLUNK. A WHIR. The number changes: **B1.**

The WHIR stops.

He looks at the floor indicator. **B1.**

Shay stares at it. Turns the key again. Again. Nothing. The indicator holds. B1.

He POUNDS the doors, twice, echoing down the hall. A picture of two smiling stick figures next to where his hand lands. 

DING. The floor indicator changes to **B2**

Shay has a moment of hope. The doors open slightly but then stall. He tries to use his fingers to pry it open with no success. 

He stares into the dark elevator, unable to see. 

CLICK. The light above him goes off.

He looks down the hall. Pitch black aside from the one sign box "LAB IN USE" glowing softly at the very end of the hall.

CLICK. The one closer turns on. Then the one closer to that.

They speed up as they come down the hallway. He looks back to the gap in the elevator.

Suddenly something BANGS against the inside of the door sending him sprawling back. 

Terrified, he abandons the elevator and runs in the other direction.

INT. B2 LOCKER ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Shay slams through the door, spins, presses it shut behind him. He looks around.

The bin sits on the scale where he left it. Lid closed. The scale readout glows in the half-light: 153.3 lbs.

He crosses to it. His hand goes to the lid. Stops. Hovers.

Inside, lying on the bags: PIKE. Folded wrong. His skin yellow, veined black. Eyes open.

Shay SCREAMS, staggers back into the lockers, CLANG.

Out in the corridor: a sensor CLICKS. Light spills under the main door.

SHF. SHF. SHF. A scrambling noise outside.

Shay presses back against the lockers, eyes on the door, and then he sees it.

At the back of the room, past the lockers: the steel sliding door. 

Shay runs toward the door. Snatches the padlock off and hauls the door sideways. It GRINDS a foot open and JAMS on its track. He turns sideways, forcing himself through the tight gap, coat scraping steel.

INT. B2 SUPPLY ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Shay hauls the door from inside. SCRAPE. It grinds to a few inches short of shut and JAMS again.

He backs down the aisle, eyes on the door and the light which is coming from underneath.

His foot catches on a box and he falls down hard.

SHF. SHF. Noises come from the locker room.

Shay looks at the glowing bulb overhead. 

He reaches up from the ground and yanks the pull-cord.

BLACK. Just the blade of light at bottom of the door pierces through on his eyes.

He backs deeper into the dark, between the shelf stacks. Presses in. Goes still. Holds his breath.

Then, through the gap: a SHADOW crosses the light. 

BANG on the door. Shay jumps. His eyes dilate.

The door slowly SCRAPES.

The gap drags wider, the grind filling the room, and in the doorway, backlit by the locker room bulb: a FIGURE.

White lab coat. Goggles. Still. Shay stares in horror.

CLICK. The light in the locker room goes off. The figure disappears.

SHAY
(barely a voice)
...Dev?

The darkness moves. Shay's breathes raggedly.

His hand finds the wall. Slaps along it and CLICKS the switch.

The bulb dimly stutters on.

The figure is still at the door. Lab coat. Goggles. And around the goggles, where a face should be: a dark blur. Smudged.

It's looking at him.

Then it comes. A dry papery ROAR of SHF SHF SHF SHF, gliding and shuddering at once, the aisle swallowed in half a second, and it STOPS, inches from his face.

A held beat.

It SCREAMS in Shay's face.

SMASH TO BLACK.

SILENCE.

TITLE ON SCREEN: "SHUFFLE. Based on a true story."

Over black: SHF. SHF. SHF.

FADE OUT.{{Slugline Document Settings
